```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <markdown.h>

/**
 * Converts markdown text to HTML.
 *
 * @param markdownText The markdown text to convert.
 * @return The HTML text.
 */
std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdownText) {
    markdown::MarkdownIn markdown(markdownText);
    markdown::MarkdownOut htmlOut;

    markdown.markdown(&markdownIn, &htmlOut);

    return htmlOut.c_str();
}

int main() {
    std::string markdownText = "# This is a heading\n\nThis is a paragraph.";
    std::string htmlText = markdownToHtml(markdownText);

    std::cout << htmlText << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

This function uses the markdown library to convert markdown text to HTML. The `markdown::MarkdownIn` object is used to parse the markdown text, and the `markdown::MarkdownOut` object is used to generate the HTML text. The `markdown.markdown` function is then used to perform the conversion.

Please note that you need to install the markdown library before you can use this function. You can install it using your package manager or by downloading it from the official website.

Also, this function assumes that the markdown text is valid and does not contain any errors. If the markdown text is invalid, the function may not work correctly.

You can install the markdown library using the following command:

```bash
sudo apt-get install libmarkdown-dev
```

Or, you can download it from the official website: https://github.com/lepture/markdown

You can also use other markdown libraries such as [github-markdown](https://github.com/guikens/markdown) or [commonmark](https://github.com/commonmark/commonmark) if you prefer.

